    <string name="peppy_mirroring">Mirroring</string>
    <string name="peppy_notification_mirroring_disclosure">Notification access lets Peppy read the content Android makes available, which may include verification codes or bank alerts. Mirroring is off by default. When you enable it, Peppy encrypts copies for your vault and stores them on your configured server for your authorized vault devices. Dismissing a mirrored notification on another device may also clear it on this phone while mirroring is permitted. Turning mirroring off stops new captures and remote phone clearing. Already-synced history stays in your vault.</string>
    <string name="peppy_sms_sync">SMS synchronization</string>
    <string name="peppy_sms_history_title">Phone message sync</string>
    <string name="peppy_sms_history_description">With SMS sync enabled, Peppy imports existing and new sent and received messages available in Android\'s SMS storage. They may include verification codes or bank alerts. Peppy encrypts copies for your vault and stores them on your configured server for access by your authorized vault devices. SMS access may also let Peppy read your SIM phone number and sync an encrypted copy for group MMS recipient matching, even if MMS capture is off. Carrier SMS itself is not end-to-end encrypted.</string>
