    <string name="peppy_permissions_sms_disclosure">With SMS sync enabled, Peppy imports existing and new sent and received messages available in Android\'s SMS storage. They may include verification codes or bank alerts. Peppy encrypts copies for your vault, stores them on your configured server and shares them with your authorized vault devices. SMS access may also let Peppy read your SIM phone number and sync an encrypted copy for group MMS recipient matching, even if MMS capture is off. Send SMS lets this phone send texts queued by those devices. Contact sync is a separate opt-in feature; Peppy does not read call logs or replace your default SMS app. Carrier SMS itself is not end-to-end encrypted.</string>
